uod|n|A crack or breach; a gap or fissure; a defect of continuity or cohesion; as, a flaw in a knife or a vase. ; A defect; a fault; as, a flaw in reputation; a flaw in a will, in a deed, or in a statute. ; A sudden burst of noise and disorder; a tumult; uproar; a quarrel. ; A sudden burst or gust of wind of short duration.	a:tkd,111,35;16dc,88,2;1dh0,79,5;wds,79,29;fq9,72,6;i7p,65,17;1zxr,63,32;idx,61,6;1bi9,59,40;1aja,51,4;20y7,42,9;27vu,39,7;1ptt,38,10;1i5s,33,4;11t2,27,2~1bi9,59,40;tkd,111,35;1zxr,63,32;wds,79,29;i7p,65,17;1ptt,38,10;20y7,42,9;27vu,39,7;idx,61,6;fq9,72,6;1pok,9,5;1ttl,24,5;1dh0,79,5;8an,22,4;1aja,51,4	V:1lp,54,3~1lp,54,3	n:cxb,76,18;tkd,70,2;l1c,66,40;1zax,58,19~l1c,66,40;1zax,58,19;cxb,76,18;tkd,70,2
