uyl|n|A current of water; a stream. ; A variable quantity, considered as increasing or diminishing; -- called, in the modern calculus, the function or integral.	a:7d1,17,1;1t6e,14,2;1f74,3,6~1f74,3,6;1t6e,14,2;7d1,17,1	v:7d4,62,5;7d1,40,5~7d4,62,5;7d1,40,5	n:22yb,36,2;22h2,23,6~22h2,23,6;22yb,36,2	N:22yf,59,3;22yd,36,1~22yf,59,3;22yd,36,1
uyl|a|Flowing or capable of flowing; liquid; glodding; easily moving. ; Ready in the use of words; voluble; copious; having words at command; and uttering them with facility and smoothness; as, a fluent speaker; hence, flowing; voluble; smooth; -- said of language; as, fluent speech.	j:vxo,69,7;22yd,62,6;22yf,59,3;qjd,26,2~vxo,69,7;22yd,62,6;22yf,59,3;qjd,26,2	e:tb2,54,8;19lo,23,4;1f74,18,17;2l1,18,4;2epf,15,8~1f74,18,17;tb2,54,8;2epf,15,8;2l1,18,4;19lo,23,4
